## Phase 162 — Root Cleanup & Temp Area Relocation

Status: Implemented — pending human commit

Goals:
  Keep the repo root free of working folders: builder scaffolding and the
  TypeScript runtime move into `.sdd/codding/` (temp/template area), all
  duplicates are resolved, and every path reference is rewritten.

Decisions:
  - Root `{be,fe,mobile}-builder/` + `Dockerfile.*-builder` were the LIVE
    referenced sources; the `.sdd/codding/` copies were unreferenced
    EOL-variant duplicates -> root copies relocated, duplicates deleted.
  - `sdd-adapter/` (73 files, product runtime) relocated to
    `.sdd/codding/sdd-adapter/`; root `Dockerfile` now ships it through
    the single existing `COPY .sdd ./.sdd` (13 redundant COPY lines
    removed) with `WORKDIR /workspace/.sdd/codding/sdd-adapter`.
  - `.sdd/projects/sddra/history/prompt-pairs.jsonl` deleted as the stale
    duplicate; canonical copy stays at `prompts/history/prompt-pairs.jsonl`
    ([R104]). `docs/assets/logo.png` is unreferenced by README/docs ->
    kept locally, ignored (per git-status-analysis decision).
  - Builder Dockerfiles simplified so they actually build (be/fe were
    unbuildable: shell redirection on COPY, missing sources).

Deliverables:
  - `.sdd/codding/` — be-builder, fe-builder, mobile-builder,
    sdd-adapter, the 3 Dockerfiles, and a README marker stating the area
    is temp/template (not product) with its harvesting rule
  - `.gitignore` — `.sdd/codding/**/{node_modules,dist,output}` + logs,
    `.sdd/projects/sddra/history/`, `docs/assets/`
  - Path fixes — Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml (3 builder refs), docs
    (contributing, install, quick-start, architecture, root README),
    `.sdd/commands/sdd-{purge,scan}.sdd` `@`-refs, MAP/STRUCTURE/
    architecture INDEX, `.claude/settings.local.json` live hooks,
    `spec-loader.ts` `.sdd` fallback, `commands-purge.test.ts` literal
  - `.sdd/codding/sdd-adapter/commands.ts` — mojibake glyphs removed from
    the [HEALTH-09] detector comments (the gate self-triggered once the
    adapter moved inside the `.sdd/` scan scope)

Validation:
  - `docker compose config` -> exit 0
  - `docker compose build sdd-sandbox be-builder fe-builder mobile-builder`
    -> all exit 0 (be/fe were unbuildable before)
  - compile-first test flow -> 32/32 test files pass, 0 failures
  - `/sdd-health` -> HEALTHY, exit 0 (0 mojibake, 0 command drift)
  - `/sdd-drift` -> 0 drifts (spec-loader resolves `.sdd` from the new
    adapter workdir)
  - `git status` — only intended changes remain (no untracked noise
    except `.sdd/codding/`, which holds the relocated sources to commit)

Blockers:
  - Human commit required: host `git add`/`commit` are permission-denied
    for agents.

## Progress Summary

Focus: Phase 130-135 - Living Engineering System

Completed:
  - Phase 130: Temporal Knowledge System (timeline/) — complete with changes/snapshots/migrations/evolution + subdirectory indexes
  - Phase 131: Task Graph & Execution Planner (tasks/ extensions) — TASK-STATE-MACHINE, LOOP-PROTECTION, SKILL-CHAIN
  - Phase 132: Multi-Agent Coordination (agent/) — core roles, specialty roles, ECC bridge, supervisor, security-rules, prompts
  - Phase 133: Semantic Engineering Graph (graph/ extensions) — model, relationships, traversal, health
  - Phase 134: Self-Evolving SDD (policies/, evolution/) — evolution pipeline, candidates/challenges/proposals/approved
  - Phase 135: SDD Query Language (queries/) — INDEX.sdd with 18 keywords, relationship syntax, 5 saved queries
  - Phase 136: Intent → Plan → Execution Graph (intents/, plans/, assumptions/) — intent lifecycle, execution modes, approval gates, assumption registry with risk levels
  - Phase 137: AI Bootstrap Protocol (bootstrap/, glossary/, system/) — 13-phase protocol, authority model, identity, handoff, glossary, context compiler, tool governance
  - Phase 138: AI Gatekeeper & Tool Governance (governance/) — 20 capabilities, permission matrix, environment policies, 15 resources with data tiers, lock protocol, trust hierarchy, security events, action journal
  - Phase 139: SDD Lifecycle & Garbage Collection (lifecycle/) — state machine (Active→Stale→Deprecated→Archived), 6 quality dimensions, garbage collector protocol, compactor, trust-aware pruning
  - ECC Framework: 67 agents → 8 core + 4 specialty roles, 281 skills, 94 commands, 35 MCP servers, 102 AgentShield rules
  - Human-readable docs: sdd-overview.md (17 commands), sdd-commands.md, ecc-integration-guide.md, deep-analysis.md
  - Unit tests: 33/33 pass, crossref tests: 3/3 pass

Current Task:
  - None — all Phase 130-137 integration work complete

Blockers:
